cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "hiltimingdiff: measured per-stage timing divergence between simulation and hardware for one PAT pipeline"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-11-16"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/OmAcharya-avtr/hiltimingdiff"
authors:
  - name: "OPTIMA Organisation"
abstract: >-
  Executes one six-stage pointing, acquisition and tracking frame pipeline in
  two modes -- simulation mode on a host and hardware mode on a Jetson Orin
  Nano -- from the same committed source file and with the same instrumented
  driver, and reports stage by stage where the simulation's declared timing
  model diverges from the board. The headline outputs are the per-stage
  divergence ratio with a bootstrap interval whose resampling unit is the pass,
  the divergence spread across stages, the rank disagreement between the
  declared and measured stage orderings as Kendall's tau-b and as an explicit
  permutation, the least and most trustworthy stages named, and the held-out
  transfer error of a single measured scaling factor. Includes a fitted
  correction for the 7.52 per cent board drift measured over the campaign,
  reported beside the raw figure, the measured share of per-stage variance that
  co-varies with core frequency at an unpinned schedutil clock, and a gate
  branch reachability census. No learned component. Research-grade; not
  flight-qualified, not certified, and not approved for operational aerospace
  use.
keywords:
  - timing-conformance
  - hardware-in-the-loop
  - schedulability
  - jetson-orin-nano
  - per-stage-timing
  - differential-testing
